  {
   "n": 7,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • Data Science & Artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0",
   "html": "<p>Consider the Taylor series <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4e/4eb7205ad48ba6895862.png\" /> centered at <em>z</em><sub>0</sub> = 2 Which of the following statements are true regarding the radius of convergence?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "If the Taylor series converges at z = 0 the radius of convergence <em>R</em> is at least 2."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "If the Taylor series converges at z = 3 the radius of convergence <em>R</em> is at least 1."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "It is possible for the Taylor series to converge at z = 0 and diverge at z = 3."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "If the Taylor series converges at z = 0, the series must converge at all points inside the disk of radius 2 around <em>z</em><sub>0</sub> = 2."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A, B, D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a, b, d)<br />\n&bull; If the Taylor series converges at z = 0 the radius of convergence must be at least the distance<br />\nfrom z<sub>0</sub> = 2 to z = 0 which is 2. So, option (a) is true.<br />\n&bull; If the Taylor series converges at z = 3 the radius of convergence must be at least the distance<br />\nfrom z<sub>0</sub> = 2 to z = 3 which is 1. So, option (b) is true.<br />\n&bull; It is impossible for the Taylor series to converge at z = 0 and diverge at z = 3 If the series<br />\nconverges at z = 0 it will also converge at all points within the disk of radius 2, meaning it<br />\nwould converge at z = 3 as well. So, option (c) is false.<br />\n&bull; If the Taylor series converges at z = 0 it will converge at all points within the disk of radius 2<br />\naround z<sub>0</sub> = 2 meaning it will also converge at points inside this radius. So, option (d) is true.</p>"
  },
