  {
   "n": 17,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • Data Science & Artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>Let f(z) be a complex function.<br />\nConsider the following two statements:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : A point z0 is a singularity of <em>f</em>(<em>z</em>) if <em>f</em>(<em>z</em>) is not analytic at z<sub>0</sub>.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : A singularity z<sub>0</sub> is called an isolated singularity if <em>f(z</em>) is analytic on the deleted disk 0 < |z – z<sub>0</sub>| < <em>r</em> for some <em>r</em> > 0.<br />\nWhich of the following is/are true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is true"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is true"
    },
